  "docs": {
    "purpose": "A diagnostic bench for one saved permit at a time. The operator pastes a permit identifier and toggles between two tabs to see the two different shapes the backend serves for that same record - the full detail payload and the flight-board payload - so the two can be compared side by side. The identifier and chosen tab live in the web address, so a particular view can be shared as a link.",
    "data_story": "It reads nothing from the database directly. Every value arrives through 2 contracts: `/api/admin/leads/inspect/[id]`, `/api/leads/flight-board/detail/[id]`. Behind those contracts, the data comes from `building_footprints`, `coa_applications`, `cost_estimates`, `entities`, `entitlements`, `lead_trades`, `lead_views`, `lifecycle_status_history`, `logic_variables`, `neighbourhoods`, `parcel_buildings`, `parcels`, `permit_parcels`, `permit_phase_transitions`, `permit_trades`, `permits`, `phase_stay_calibration`, `scope_intensity_matrix`, `trade_forecasts`, `trades`, `universal_stream_catalog` and `user_profiles`.",
    "under_126": "**RE-PROJECT** — it writes nothing and holds no Layer-3 store, so the move is short — the server already assembles the payload and only the rendering is client-side. It renders through the DETAIL renderer (one entity, a single-param query key, declared sections), reading by reference: `/api/admin/leads/inspect/[id]`, `/api/leads/flight-board/detail/[id]`. Its `owns.components[]` declares `src/components/admin/FlightJobDetailInspector.tsx`."
  },
